Package: gitguard
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: git, python3 (>= 3.9)
Section: vcs
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/jbcayrou/gitguard
Bugs: https://github.com/jbcayrou/gitguard/issues
Description: refuse to run git on a repository changed behind your back
 gitguard fingerprints what git executes or reads as configuration in a
 repository (.git/config, hooks, attributes, nested gitdirs, the files the
 config names) and refuses to run git when it has changed since you last
 trusted it: code in a sandbox that has the repository mounted writes
 into .git/, and the next git on the host would run it.
 .
 This package installs gitguard as /usr/bin/git and as git's exec path
 entry /usr/lib/git-core/git, so that every git on the machine and every
 child git is checked; the real binaries are diverted to git.real
 (dpkg-divert) and come back when the package is removed. Each user then
 runs "gitguard trust" once in the repositories that already exist.
